{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Identity Element.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Identity Element.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"identity element identity element","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Identity Element.md","fileName":"Identity Element.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Identity Element","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Number Systems and Arithmetic]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Number Systems and Arithmetic","Opposite Number","Reciprocal","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Identity Element.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Identity Element.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"identity element identity element","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Identity Element.md","fileName":"Identity Element.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Identity Element","heading":"Identity Element","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An identity element leaves every value unchanged under a particular operation. Zero is the additive identity because\n\n$$a+0=0+a=a,$$\n\nand one is the multiplicative identity because\n\n$$a\\cdot1=1\\cdot a=a.$$\n\nIdentity is operation-specific: zero does not act as the multiplicative identity, and one does not act as the additive identity. These elements support inverse operations. An [[Opposite Number]] combines with its original through addition to reach zero, while a [[Reciprocal]] combines through multiplication to reach one.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Number Systems and Arithmetic","Opposite Number","Reciprocal","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Identity Element.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Identity Element.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"identity element identity element","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Identity Element.md","fileName":"Identity Element.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Identity Element","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Number Systems and Arithmetic","Opposite Number","Reciprocal","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}